WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.340
A little over a week ago I made a video titled
25 Things You Missed In The Stephen King's

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.340
IT Trailer.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.580
Here's a link if you missed it.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.170
And in that video I asked you guys to offer
up your input in the comments and I got an

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.640
amazing response.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.260
You all had a lot of insightful thoughts about
the trailer and things I didn't catch in my

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.260
initial video.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.820
I've also been rereading the book, and it's
been making me appreciate the finer details

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.990
of the trailer even more.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:29.419
I read through all the comments on that video,
which, at the time of writing, there are over

00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:34.860
1,000, so HUGE thank you for all the support
on that one; and I picked out some favorites

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.770
to talk about in this video.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:41.480
Now a lot of you had interesting ideas about
the meaning behind all the astronomy references,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.760
and I'm going to save those theories for the
end of this video because they may go into

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.980
spoiler territory, at least for the book,
but don't worry, I'll give you a spoiler alert

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.160
before we get there.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.940
Here are 12 Things I Missed In The Stephen
King's IT Trailer.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.870
The biggest thing I missed in my initial video
was the setting.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.490
This upcoming film actually takes place in
the 80s.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:04.970
Apologies for that misinformation on my part
and thank you to each and every one of you

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:09.490
that pointed this out in the comments -- all
2 billion of you, thank you for pointing out

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.190
that this movie takes place in the 80s.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:18.740
A couple of you let me know that more specifically,
the film takes place in 1989 and this is backed

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.930
up by the technology you see in the trailer,
and the fact that you can just look it up

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:23.930
online.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.050
It takes place in the 80s.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:30.130
But what's more interesting to me is why the
filmmakers have chosen the 80s for this film.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.820
Many of you confirmed my suspicion that the
book will be split into two movies, meaning

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:39.430
that the second movie will take place in 2016,
the same year that Part 1 was in production.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.200
When you consider the fact that the first
movie is technically a flashback, that kind

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.780
of makes this whole reboot series a modern
day remake of IT, an interesting choice when

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:52.479
you consider the significance of creepy clowns
in our culture today, such as the Staten Island

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.780
clown and his many copycats over the last
few years.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.150
We'll see if that plays into the second film
at all.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:02.030
I'll never forget that scene in the adult
portion of the mini-series where Ben notices

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:07.090
Pennywise on the side of the road; something
that seemed to happen quite a lot in October

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.590
2016.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:09.700
This is our next item.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.280
The film is scheduled to release September
8, 2017.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.930
You might be wondering, "CZ, how did you miss
this?

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.090
It says it right there!"

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:21.980
Well, it's not the release date that I missed,
but rather, the significance behind it.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:27.280
In the story, IT returns to the town every
27 years to terrorize Derry.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.910
Commenter CynicalCatLady points out, "the
first screen adaptation of IT was first aired

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:37.690
in 1990, and twenty-seven years later, the
infamous dancing clown is re-emerging to breathe

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:42.510
fresh terror into a new generation, just as
he does in the novel."

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.790
To me, that's so cool.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:48.430
That's perfect timing for a new movie, I love
when movies take real time into account.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.860
In my video, I mention how Pennywise's eyes
don't show up in the reflection.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.680
Some of you mentioned that this could just
be because the eyes are enhanced in visual

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.410
effects and they just didn't want to do the
effect in the reflection as well.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.599
That is something that crossed my mind, having
done quite a bit of visual effects myself,

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:07.750
but then I saw this comment, which doesn't
make any sense, but it got me thinking about

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.550
the novel, and how IT doesn't have a shadow.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:15.180
So maybe no eyes in the reflection is the
film manifestation of that, or at the very

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.730
least, one of those choices that's easy to
make because you know it's going to save you

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.060
a lot of money in visual effects.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.150
Oftentimes the reasoning for a choice made
in a film is something simple like that.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:28.830
For example, I questioned what that key might
be around Beverly's neck.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:34.400
A commenter named WhenTheSkyTurnsDark points
out that it may just be her house key, which

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.790
she needs to keep with her because, unlike
many of the others, she might not have someone

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.540
at home who can let her in all the time.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.940
We already know her Dad is unreliable, and
she may use the necklace for the key because

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.190
her Dad would beat her if she ever lost it.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.610
Here's another thing I got wrong.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:52.700
I pointed out these flower beds in the wide
shot and said they were arrows.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.849
Many of you took a closer look and discovered
that they are actually crosses.

00:03:55.849 --> 00:04:00.130
While we are on this landscape shot, I have
to admire the choice of location.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:05.050
This is a town called Port Hope in Ontario,
Canada, one of three Canadian cities where

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.400
the movie was filmed.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.819
You can see much more clearly here that they
are indeed crosses, and as a couple of you

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:13.880
speculated, that that's because of the church
right across the street.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.909
The park over here is called Memorial Park,
and I'm sure there are plenty of Memorial

00:04:17.909 --> 00:04:22.530
Parks across North America, but that is also
the name of an often mentioned location in

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.960
Derry in the book.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:27.660
It's more of a coincidence than anything that
would be super important to the movie, but

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.910
I found it interesting nonetheless.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:33.910
Another useless but interesting location I
noticed was right across the street from Memorial

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.780
Park, there's a restaurant called Turtle John's.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:41.250
There are constant references to "The Turtle"
the novel, and I'll actually discuss that

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.750
in more detail a bit later on in the video.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.780
There's also this canal, which will play the
part of the offshoot of the Kenduskeag Stream

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.400
that runs through Derry.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.120
Not only is that where Ben first meets Pennywise
in the book, but I was checking out some photos

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.690
of the canal and it's shallow enough to wade
in, so I wouldn't be surprised if this also

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.460
the location for The Barrens, which if you
aren't familiar with IT, is the place where

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.120
the group basically bonds and becomes friends
when they get in trouble for building a dam

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.120
downstream.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.403
Again, it's not like a dealbreaker for the
movie, but it's just a nice touch to see when

00:05:10.403 --> 00:05:14.620
locations are actually connected in a film,
especially one that focuses so much on the

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.770
town it's located in and has scenes that move
from location to location.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:22.139
There's also a library right in the center
of town here, which brings me to the next

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:23.139
thing I missed.

00:05:23.139 --> 00:05:27.970
So in the mini-series, Richie has his confrontation
with Pennywise in the library, which is obviously

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.330
an iconic scene.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.490
In the novel however, it's Ben who spends
all of his time at the library, especially

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.850
before he becomes friends with the other 6
kids.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:40.520
He is at the library on the last day of school,
which is what it would seem they are depicting

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:41.520
here.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.449
For the record, in the book, he's also the
one who goes back to the library as an adult,

00:05:45.449 --> 00:05:48.650
seeing as how it was like his safe haven from
the bullies as a child.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:52.139
This flooded basement scene in the trailer
sparked some debate in the comments as to

00:05:52.139 --> 00:05:53.770
whose basement it was.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:57.509
I naturally thought it was the Denborough
basement just because Bill is down there by

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:59.990
himself, when he encounters the illusion of
Georgie.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:02.600
Some people suggested it could be the 29 Neibolt
basement.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.949
I don't think that's too likely considering
the modern appliances seen here, and this

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:10.710
guy TaylorTV brings up another good point,
which is that it would make sense that he

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:14.770
encounters Georgie in the cellar, because
in the first chapter, Bill sends him down

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.630
there to get the turtle wax, which we'll get
back to, essentially sending him to his own

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.919
doom in a way.

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:25.210
So IT takes advantage of this by using Georgie's
image in the basement to guilt his brother.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.880
Seems like a logical way of looking at it.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.580
OK, so before I get into the astronomy stuff,
there were a few things that people brought

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.960
up, that were not things that I missed, but
things that I didn't really think anyone would

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.680
miss, so I'll just list those off real quick.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.780
This could be the Leper that Eddie sees at
29 Neibolt.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:42.840
This could be a depiction of the Black Spot
fire.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.800
It also might be a replacement for the junkyard
bird scene.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.229
I actually wouldn't really mind if it was.

00:06:48.229 --> 00:06:51.740
Bill doesn't stutter at all in the trailer,
but I'm not too worried about that, I feel

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.940
like the trailer was just cut with good audio
from him to make it flow better.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.651
OK with that out of the way, this next part
is going to contain some spoilers for the

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:03.460
book regarding the origin of IT, so if you
don't want hear, I'll see you in the next

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.460
video.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.810
Assuming we both survive....

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.320
OK.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.040
So You guys have been telling me that you
think the astronomy stuff is a reference to

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.390
the fact that IT came to Earth from outer
space.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:19.150
This ties into the whole subplot about how
IT is basically the Stephen King demon, and

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:23.430
how the counterbalance is The Turtle, which
is like the creator of all things.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.440
I'm not going to dig too deep into the lore
for the sake of simplicity, but basically

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.190
what you need to know is that both IT and
The Turtle come from this void in outer space.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:35.820
Looking at the trailer with that information,
I started to notice even more references to

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.620
outer space scattered throughout Derry.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.580
There were some people in the comments who
were not buying into this because of the fact

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.500
that in the first scene with the Denborough
brothers, Bill seems to sealed Georgie's boat

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.630
with Gulf Wax, as opposed to the Turtle Wax
that Georgie fetches from the cellar in the

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.630
book.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.750
So their argument is that the filmmakers only
really have a reason to do this if they are

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.250
not going to feature the turtle and the ritual
and stuff.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:57.790
I don't think this will be the case.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:02.849
The ending of the TV mini-series is widely
considered it's weakest point, and it doesn't

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:04.020
include the ritual.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.050
Also, with this movie taking place in a different
decade, it stands to reason that different

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.310
products would be more relevant in another
time period.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:15.039
And with the new time period comes a new audience
and new fans.

